# Copy this file to .env (same folder, the repository root) and fill in your own values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored. Never commit real keys, never paste them into a chat, and never "source" this file:
# the programs read it themselves (python-dotenv), and a value with a space would break a shell.
# Rotate every key at the end of the project.

# --- Alpaca PAPER account (https://app.alpaca.markets, paper trading) -------------------------------------
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional. Leave empty for the paper host. Any non-paper host is refused by the broker module.
ALPACA_TRADING_URL=

# --- NewsAPI (https://newsapi.org) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEWSAPI_KEY=
# Optional. Most requests per UTC day for the per-symbol news tool. Default 80 (free plan allows 100).
# NEWSAPI_DAILY_LIMIT=80

# --- Groq (LLM for the Bull, Bear, Judge, News and Reflection agents) ----------------------------------------
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Broker mode ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# offline      sample account from trading_system/fixtures (the default when this is empty)
# alpaca_paper read the real paper account
# It can be set here or on the command line. Placing orders needs more switches (see below).
BROKER_MODE=offline

# --- Local dashboard (python -m trading_system.web.server) -----------------------------------------------------
# The Keys page of the dashboard writes your name and keys to this file for you (TRADER_NAME is the name shown in
# the page header). Live paper placement is NOT a setting here: start the dashboard with --live in the terminal.
# TRADER_NAME=

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder for the raw-bar and news disk cache. Default: trading_system/data_cache (git-ignored).
# TRADING_DATA_CACHE_DIR=

# --- Order switches: DO NOT PUT THESE IN THIS FILE --------------------------------------------------------------
# They are safety gates and must be typed on the command line for the one command that needs them, e.g.
#   ALPACA_ORDERS_ENABLED=true BROKER_MODE=alpaca_paper python -m trading_system.crew.run_cycle AAPL --approve AAPL --submit
# ALPACA_ORDERS_ENABLED   master switch for sending paper orders (off unless it is exactly "true")
# ALPACA_STOPS_ENABLED    also attach a protective stop to each live BUY (off unless it is exactly "true")
# They are listed here only as comments, on purpose.

# --- Local dashboard launch settings (do not put live mode in .env) ------------------------------
# PAPER_WEB_PORT=8765
# PAPER_WEB_LIVE_MODE=true must be set in the process launch environment, never here.
